  "_commit": {
    "id": "76c40872c2f5ada2d4fb490347872cc7f29c0155",
    "author": "tgirke <tgirke@citrus.ucr.edu>",
    "committer": "tgirke <tgirke@citrus.ucr.edu>",
    "message": "Wire the vignette's two Ensembl chunks into the live-API fallback\n\nThe ensembl_paralogs and ensembl_orthologs chunks called the homology\nendpoint unguarded, the only remaining vignette chunks doing live work\nwithout a fallback. Ensembl degrades to an empty result plus a warning\nrather than an error, so an outage never failed the build - it just\npublished two empty tables, which is the quieter and worse outcome.\n\nBoth chunks now use .dtiLiveOrCached() with the fixtures that already\nship for them (ensembl_paralogs_nlrp3.rds,\nensembl_orthologs_nlrp3_mouse.rds), matching the fields_all and\nlegacy_run_everything chunks, and print the same cached-results note\nwhen the fallback fires.\n\nVerified both ways: live right now returns 20 paralog rows and 1 mouse\northolog with dtiCached FALSE; under a simulated total outage (.dtiApiGET\nforced to signal failure) both recover the identical rows from the\nfixtures with dtiCached TRUE and the note shown.\n",
    "time": 1786838642
  },
